# --- de-identification artefacts: NEVER commit ---
# uid_map.jsonl holds SOURCE DICOM UIDs and is PHI-equivalent.
# deid_secret.key is the only means of re-identification.
.deid/
.deid-*/
*.key
uid_map.jsonl
backups/

# --- datasets: never vendored into this repo ---
# Public data: cite the TCIA DOI. Private clinical data: never leaves the clinic's control.
data/
datasets/
*.dcm
*.nrrd
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.mrml

# --- recorded fixtures (generated DICOM derived from patient studies) ---
# Copied out from under `spikes/week0/out/` before that directory was deleted, because a
# fixture belongs to the test that reads it and should not be the last thing keeping a
# directory alive. They are recordings the week-0 spike produced FROM patient studies, so
# they are not redistributable and are in no clone; `tests/_support/skips.py` declares
# them as the `recorded-fixtures` corpus and the tests that read them skip rather than
# fail when they are absent.
#
# The five `spikes/**` lines that used to follow are gone with the directory. They covered
# `out/`, two generations of fixture tree and the mutation scratch -- 62 MB of regenerable
# binary that `verify_roundtrip.py fixture` rebuilt. Nothing rebuilds it now; what the
# suite still needs is the JSON above, which is why it was copied out rather than ignored
# one more time.
tests/_recorded/
*-report.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# transient test-evidence dumps
.ev-*.txt
.evidence-*.txt
.evidence/
medos.egg-info/

# --- trained model artefacts: never committed ---
# A bundle is 392 MB for a conv U-Net and 4.1 GB for SegResNetDS (356M parameters). Weights belong
# in an artifact store addressed by digest, not in git history: `MOS-REG-084` carries a ModelVersion
# as OCI layers, and a bundle's identity is its `bundle_digest`, which `result.json` records.
artifacts/
